A||N||6||2xsess||Just picked up my "new" 85GT||||10||
Z||000000||2xsess||09-16-2000||01:29 AM||||WOW, I just drove my 85GT home,4 hour drive and man I realized how much I missed the Fiero. Just hearing that rumble as I accelerated onto I-95 made me smile like a school boy. <P>The car hasn't really been driven for @6 months, but the gentleman that I bought it off of really helped me out, he had the oil changed,put in a new O2 sensor,PCV valve, and fixed one of the boots that had slipped off the CV joint. <P>I would love to post some beautiful pics but the only ones I have are of it at his place all dirty, plus pip doesn't seem to work for me. <BR> <A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/2xsess85GT_8.jpg" TARGET=_blank>www.fiero.nl/uploads/2xsess85GT_8.jpg</A>  <BR> <A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Mvc-006s.jpg" TARGET=_blank>www.fiero.nl/uploads/Mvc-006s.jpg</A>   Interior pics.<P>We also discovered that whoever owned the car before had cut the wires going to the speed pickup and the other end seems to have disappeared. I have to get a manual with schematics and trace where the wires go.If anyone has any tips I appreciate it. <P><BR>Thanks,<BR>Jeff<BR>85GT <P>[This message has been edited by 2xsess (edited 09-16-2000).]<P>[This message has been edited by 2xsess (edited 09-16-2000).]<p>[This message has been edited by 2xsess (edited 09-16-2000).]||||reg||10
Z||000001||trigger||09-16-2000||06:22 PM||||Nice find.  How many fieros does he have?<P>------------------<BR>Honestly officer, I was just keeping up with the flow of traffic.  I know there aren't any cars in the area, that's how far behind I am.||||reg||1
Z||000002||2xsess||09-16-2000||06:27 PM||||He said he usually has four or five whole ones sitting arround. He has a 7100mile 87GT with wood int and MrMikes seats that is super sweet,but $10,500 was a little steep for my budget. He is located near Daytona. <P>I actually just followed my wife in the van to make sure I didn't get going too fast.....too fast whats that???<P>Jeff||||reg||10
Z||000003||2xsess||09-17-2000||04:06 AM||||Also the check engine light kept coming on but today after I put new plugs,wires,cap,and rotor on it and fixed the speedometer it stopped.<P>Jeff<BR>85GT||||reg||1
Z||000004||sdm1964||09-17-2000||10:59 AM||||Jeff we got to get together, I live in glennville, I think I know the guy you bought the car from.Wow this is too cool to have 2 white gt's running around post.||||reg||1
Z||000005||2xsess||09-17-2000||07:29 PM||||I finally got up the courage to pull the e-brake on today and lo and behold it works. This is a first for me. every Fiero I've ever bought I had to fix the e-brake.||||reg||1
Z||000006||Shadow Wolf||09-21-2000||02:54 AM||||When I picked up my '87 GT I was told that the e-brake didn't work....So I never really gave it at though at first, but at one point on the drive home I stopped somewhere, on a hill and just for the heck of it, pulled the  brake... IT WORKED!  Turns out they figured the brake didn't work because the handle went back down to the floor after it was applied.<P>Heh, that was a funny drive home.  Only an hour and a half, but I had a friend of mine drive my white sprint back, but I forgot to tell him I needed to bleed some air from the brake lines.  Needless to say, he didn't appriciate that. <BR>(Of course, the wheel alignment was also out a bit, caused an annoying vibration, among other things. &lt;BG&gt; )<BR>||||reg||1
